{"page_id": "olmo_arxiv_math-2503.06293_pg24-p1", "markdown": "with the contours T1. It is found that, when grade restricting the branes of Eq. (4.7) to a specific window, the open Witten index was consistent when calculated on the positive\n\nphase and on the negative phase, i.e. XL.N = XE.N, suggesting strongly that successful brane\n\ntransport has taken place. The results of a few examples are presented below.\n\nFor KGr(2,1), the basis of branes used was {(0,0), (1,0), (1,1), (2, 0), (2, 1), (2,2)} and the\n\nopen Witten indices was calculated to be\n\n10\n\n4\n\n20\n\n20\n\n16 20\n\n-6\n\n-4\n\n4\n\n- 10\n\n-4\n\n4\n\n10\n\n-20\n\n- 4\n- 6\n- 4\n- 10\n- 4\n\n-16\n\n-20\n\nー20\n\n（4.14）\n\nA special note is needed here: this was found to be consistent for a set of branes all grade restricted to one of the charge window types in Fig. 1. On the other hand, if a set of branes grade restricted to different window types were mixed together, so that the entire set was not grade restricted to the same charge window type, then the open Witten indices was found to be inconsistent. Thus it is believed that branes must be grade restricted in exactly the same way when computing the Witten index, despite multiple ways of charge restriction being valid for a single choice of theta-angle.\n\nFor KGr(2,5), the basis of branes used was\n\n((0,0), (1,0), (1,1), (2,0), (2,1), (2,2), (3,0), (3,1), (3,2), (3,3)} Then we found'\n\n- 40\n- 15\n\n- 10\n- 15\n\nx5= X2.5=\n\n0510154050351515\n\n야0os00k\n\n-40\n\n-50\n\n-35\n\n丝g99900\n\n175\n\n175\n\n50 105\n\n40\n\n10\n\n9S1s00og0\n\n顺两1场5050515\n\n아비회\n\n-50\n\n第号1第151\n\n（4.15）\n\nFor KGr(2,6), we have 15 generators so, we just present the computation for the subset\n\n{(0,0), (1,0), (1, L), (2,1), (2,2), (3,2), (3,3), (1,3), (4,4)):\n\n- 36\n- 70\n- 15\n\n-420\n\n3฿6-a\n\n15\n\n70\n\n105\n\n420\n\n190\n\n1764\n\n1764\n\n36\n\n70\n\n315\n\n420\n\n1624\n\n1764\n\n-15\n\n-315\n\n-70\n\n-490\n\n-420\n\n- 105\n\n1o0฿3\n\n105\n\n420\n\n19